[2026-02-04T17:59:00.877Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TWsN6dMPM6rbqBZPs3W46V","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Russia territorial demands Ukraine peace negotiations 2026 Donetsk region\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"The U.K. and France would install 'military hubs' in Ukraine as part of a peace plan\",\"url\":\"https://www.npr.org/2026/01/06/g-s1-104730/progress-ukraine-talks-paris-uncertain\"},{\"title\":\"Clarifying Territorial Disputes in Ukraine | Russia Matters\",\"url\":\"https://www.russiamatters.org/analysis/clarifying-territorial-disputes-ukraine\"},{\"title\":\"Rubio Says Work Under Way to Resolve 'Very Difficult' Donetsk Issue in Ukraine Peace Talks\",\"url\":\"https://www.usnews.com/news/world/articles/2026-01-28/rubio-says-territorial-issue-over-donetsk-yet-to-be-bridged-between-russia-ukraine\"},{\"title\":\"Ukraine’s top allies meet in Paris to push for Kyiv’s security guarantees | Russia-Ukraine war News | Al Jazeera\",\"url\":\"https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/1/6/ukraines-top-allies-meet-in-paris-to-push-for-kyivs-security-guarantees\"},{\"title\":\"Peace negotiations in the Russo-Ukrainian war (2022–present) - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peace_negotiations_in_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(2022%E2%80%93present)\"},{\"title\":\"Russia, Ukraine to hold trilateral peace talks with U.S. for first time\",\"url\":\"https://www.nbcnews.com/world/ukraine/russia-ukraine-triateral-peace-talks-trump-envoy-putin-kremlin-rcna255546\"},{\"title\":\"Ukraine peace talks - House of Commons Library\",\"url\":\"https://commonslibrary.parliament.uk/research-briefings/cbp-10411/\"},{\"title\":\"Russia Analytical Report, Dec. 22, 2025–Jan. 5, 2026 | Russia Matters\",\"url\":\"https://www.russiamatters.org/news/russia-analytical-report/russia-analytical-report-dec-22-2025-jan-5-2026\"},{\"title\":\"Ukraine-Russia-US hold talks in Abu Dhabi with territory as key issue | Russia-Ukraine war News | Al Jazeera\",\"url\":\"https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/1/23/ukraine-russia-us-talks-open-in-abu-dhabi-with-territory-as-key-issue\"},{\"title\":\"Full article: Ukraine–Russia peace plans: historical lessons, operationalising criteria, and comparative assessment\",\"url\":\"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/21647259.2025.2585235\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what's happening with Russia's territorial demands regarding the Donetsk region in the 2026 Ukraine peace negotiations:\n\n## Russia's Territorial Demands\n\nPutin's demand that Ukraine surrender the 20% it still holds of Donetsk, about 5,000 sq km (1,900 sq miles), has proven a major stumbling block to any deal. More broadly, Russia is pushing for full control of eastern Ukraine's Donbas area as part of a deal.\n\n## Current State of Territory\n\nMoscow controls all of its Luhansk region, but Kyiv still holds a significant part of its Donetsk region, where attritional fighting is ongoing. According to recent analysis, 11% of the Donbas region (which is 22% of the oblast of Donetsk) remains under Ukrainian control.\n\n## Negotiations Status\n\nThere is active work under way to reconcile the territorial issue of Donetsk at U.S.-mediated talks to end Russia's war in Ukraine, with U.S. Secretary of State Marco Rubio describing the disagreement as a key remaining issue that is \"very difficult\" to resolve.\n\n## Ukraine's Position\n\nKyiv has said it will not gift Russia territory that Moscow has failed to win on the battlefield. Polls show little appetite among Ukrainians for territorial concessions.\n\nThe territorial dispute over Donetsk remains one of the central obstacles to reaching a peace agreement in 2026.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ffdb2836-5730-4184-8318-1c286009c5ec","uuid":"9bd74fad-6994-44c5-bda1-dca715c7889e","tool_use_result