ussia peace plans: historical lessons, operationalising criteria, and comparative assessment","url":"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/21647259.2025.2585235"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what's happening with Russia's territorial demands regarding the Donetsk region in the 2026 Ukraine peace negotiations:\n\n## Russia's Territorial Demands\n\nPutin's demand that Ukraine surrender the 20% it still holds of Donetsk, about 5,000 sq km (1,900 sq miles), has proven a major stumbling block to any deal. More broadly, Russia is pushing for full control of eastern Ukraine's Donbas area as part of a deal.\n\n## Current State of Territory\n\nMoscow controls all of its Luhansk region, but Kyiv still holds a significant part of its Donetsk region, where attritional fighting is ongoing. According to recent analysis, 11% of the Donbas region (which is 22% of the oblast of Donetsk) remains under Ukrainian control.\n\n## Negotiations Status\n\nThere is active work under way to reconcile the territorial issue of Donetsk at U.S.-mediated talks to end Russia's war in Ukraine, with U.S. Secretary of State Marco Rubio describing the disagreement as a key remaining issue that is \"very difficult\" to resolve.\n\n## Ukraine's Position\n\nKyiv has said it will not gift Russia territory that Moscow has failed to win on the battlefield. Polls show little appetite among Ukrainians for territorial concessions.\n\nThe territorial dispute over Donetsk remains one of the central obstacles to reaching a peace agreement in 2026."],"durationSeconds":7.404347399999999}}
[2026-02-04T17:59:01.321Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013RwbwLLAmKc6pqhKNbE5YJ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Ukraine territorial control current map Donetsk Luhansk 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"The Russia-Ukraine War Report Card, Dec. 23, 2025 | Russia Matters\",\"url\":\"https://www.russiamatters.org/news/russia-ukraine-war-report-card/russia-ukraine-war-report-card-dec-23-2025\"},{\"title\":\"Territorial control during the Russo-Ukrainian war - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Territorial_control_during_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war\"},{\"title\":\"The Russia-Ukraine War Report Card, Dec. 17, 2025 | Russia Matters\",\"url\":\"https://www.russiamatters.org/news/russia-ukraine-war-report-card/russia-ukraine-war-report-card-dec-17-2025\"},{\"title\":\"Clarifying Territorial Disputes in Ukraine | Russia Matters\",\"url\":\"https://www.russiamatters.org/analysis/clarifying-territorial-disputes-ukraine\"},{\"title\":\"Russian-occupied territories of Ukraine - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russian-occupied_territories_of_Ukraine\"},{\"title\":\"Russian Offensive Campaign Assessment, January 30, 2026 | Critical Threats\",\"url\":\"https://www.criticalthreats.org/analysis/russian-offensive-campaign-assessment-january-30-2026\"},{\"title\":\"Stats — War Mapper\",\"url\":\"https://www.warmapper.org/stats\"},{\"title\":\"The Russia-Ukraine War Report Card, Oct. 29, 2025 | Russia Matters\",\"url\":\"https://www.russiamatters.org/news/russia-ukraine-war-report-card/russia-ukraine-war-report-card-oct-29-2025\"},{\"title\":\"Russian Offensive Campaign Assessment, December 22, 2025 | Critical Threats\",\"url\":\"https://www.criticalthreats.org/analysis/russian-offensive-campaign-assessment-december-22-2025\"},{\"title\":\"DeepStateMAP | Map of the war in Ukraine\",\"url\":\"https://deepstatemap.live/en\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's the current territorial control situation in Donetsk and Luhansk as of early 2026:\n\n## Current Control Status\n\nAs of October 28, 2025, Russia controlled 99% of Luhansk region and 72% of Donetsk region. More recent assessments indicate similar control levels.\n\nRussia essentially controls all of Luhansk and 78% of Donetsk, with approximately 2,250 square miles of Donetsk still held by Ukrainian forces—11% of the Donbas region (22% of Donetsk oblast).\n\n## Overall Territorial Loss\n\nSince the full-scale invasion began on February 24, 2022, Russia has gained approximately 28,949 square miles (12% of Ukraine), and now controls about 45,574 square miles (20% of Ukraine) including Crimea and pre-invasion seizures.\n\n## Recent Developments\n\nIn the period of November 18–December 16, 2025, Russian forces gained 215 square miles of Ukrainian territory, continuing a pattern of gradual territorial gains.\n\nThe situation remains a key point of contention in peace negotiations, with territorial control of Donetsk Oblast being described as a central issue in ongoing diplomatic efforts.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ffdb2836-5730-4184-8318-1c286009c5ec","uuid":"504e67d5-5bd9-4722-b1d4-6cc8aa76bd31","tool_use_result":{"query":"Ukraine territorial control current map Donetsk Luhansk 2026","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01YA5BaruYqX1SGNPT3wMtrc","content":[{"title":"The Russia-Ukraine War Report Card, Dec. 23, 2025 | Russia Matters","url":"https://www.russiamatters.org/news/russia-ukraine-war-report-card/russia-ukraine-war-report-card-dec-23-2025"},{"title":"Territorial control during the Russo-Ukrainian war - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Territorial_control_during_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war"},{"title":"The Russia-Ukraine War Report Card, Dec. 17, 2025 | Russia Matters","url":"https://www.russiamatters.org/news/russia-ukraine-war-report-card/russ